# The end-to-end harness drives real legacy clients inside emulators. This tree
# commits only OUR sources (the per-platform test tools, scripts, docs). The
# heavyweight third-party pieces are fetched/installed locally, never committed:
#
#   tools/   — emulators (86box, minivmac, snow), the MSVC 1.x/NT SDK kits,
#              flopgen, mtools, MPW/SDK disk images and archives (~1.2 GB).
#   tmp/     — scratch space for the host-side build/pack steps.
#
# and all build outputs (objects, linked binaries, floppy images, CMake trees,
# generated script.txt copies) are regenerated by the per-platform build steps.

# --- Downloaded tooling & scratch (never committed) --------------------------
# Ignore everything directly under /tools/ (86box, minivmac, snow, mtools,
# flopgen, disk images, SDK archives — ~1.2 GB) but NOT /tools/ itself, so the
# MSVC re-include below can take effect. (A blanket "/tools/" would exclude the
# directory outright and git would never descend into it to see the negation.)
/tools/*
/tmp/

# (The specific tooling to keep is re-included at the bottom of this file, after
# all other rules, so those negations have the last word.)

# --- Build outputs -----------------------------------------------------------
# Scoped to our source dirs on purpose: a global *.exe/*.obj/*.lib would also
# strip the pinned MSVC kit above (its compilers ARE .exe/.lib files), so we
# only ignore artifacts where WE build — windows/{win16,win32} and macos/build*.
windows/win16/*.obj
windows/win16/*.exe
windows/win16/*.EXE
windows/win16/*.img
windows/win16/*.map
windows/win16/*.MAP
windows/win32/*.obj
windows/win32/*.exe
windows/win32/*.EXE
windows/win32/*.img
windows/win32/*.map
windows/win32/*.MAP

# CMake build trees (macOS AFPE2E)
macos/build/
macos/build-*/

# Generated at pack time from scripts/*.txt — the source of truth is scripts/
# (paths are relative to this .gitignore's dir, hence the windows/ prefix).
windows/win16/script.txt
windows/win32/script.txt

# Per-run output written next to the .EXE
results.txt

# --- Pin legacy tooling that must travel with the repo (LAST word) -----------
# The repo-root .gitignore ignores *.exe and *.dll, and /tools/* above ignores
# these dirs; these negations come after every other rule so they win. Each is
# pinned in-repo because it is small, effectively unobtainable, and required to
# build/pack the e2e floppies — committed verbatim, artifact-extension or not.
#
#   msvc/    — legacy MSVC 1.x/NT compilers/linkers (CL/LINK/C1/C2, runtime DLLs)
#   mtools/  — FAT12 image manipulation (mcopy/mformat...) + source tarball
#   flopgen  — the floppy-image packer (win + posix binaries) + source tarball
#   mpw/     — MPW-GM.img.bin: Apple's real Universal Interfaces (MacBinary
#              DiskCopy image), fed to the Retro68 container as INTERFACESFILE
#              so AppleTalk.h resolves — Retro68's own free "multiversal"
#              interfaces don't implement pre-System-7 APIs like AppleTalk yet.
#
# Still ignored: the emulators (86box, minivmac, snow) and other MPW/SDK disk
# images and archives.
!/tools/msvc/
!/tools/msvc/**
!/tools/mtools/
!/tools/mtools/**
!/tools/flopgen
!/tools/flopgen.exe
!/tools/Flopgen-0.1.0.tar.gz
!/tools/mpw/
!/tools/mpw/**
